{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.CrossingGradedModel","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CrossingGradedModel","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.MassGapKeystone"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.instHasYangMillsMassGapCrossingGraded","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.instHasYangMillsMassGapCrossingGraded","kind":"instance","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CrossingGradedModel.lean#L135-L155","doc":"The millennium-conjecture class `HasYangMillsMassGap` is\n**non-vacuous in-framework**: the crossing-graded model\ninstantiates it on the substrate window.  (First in-framework\ninstance; MODEL caveat per the module docstring.)\n\nThe class's `mass_gap_holds : Prop` field carries the mass-gap\nproposition for the model transfer matrix,\n`(crossingGradedTM …).hasMassGap`, and `gap_present` is discharged by\nthe model's `crossingGradedYMG.gap_positive` (the crossing-graded gap\nis positive by `minCrossingEnergy_pos`).  MODEL CAVEAT (as above): this\nis the crossing-graded model spectrum, not the physical `End(Aₙ)`\ntransfer matrix — the physical Yang–Mills mass gap remains open. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.crossingGradedYMG","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.crossingGradedYMG","kind":"def","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CrossingGradedModel.lean#L110-L133","doc":"**Per-level Yang–Mills mass-gap witness for the model**: on\n`1 < q ≤ 2`, the crossing-graded model satisfies the\n`YangMillsMassGap` interface — `massGapBound q ≤ gapValue = E_×(q)`\n(since `(q−1)² ≤ 1` there) and the gap is positive.\n\nMODEL CAVEAT: this witnesses the *conjecture interface* for the\ncrossing-graded model spectrum, not for the physical `End(Aₙ)`\ntransfer matrix.  See module docstring. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.crossingGraded_substrateGap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.crossingGraded_substrateGap","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CrossingGradedModel.lean#L100-L108","doc":"**The model tower carries the uniform substrate gap** on the\nsubstrate window `1 < q ≤ 2` — the full S1b/S1c pipeline composed:\ncrossing-graded construction ⟹ `CrossingFiltration` ⟹\n`SubstrateGap`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.crossingGradedTM_filtration","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.crossingGradedTM_filtration","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CrossingGradedModel.lean#L80-L98","doc":"**The model satisfies the crossing-energy filtration** — by\nconstruction: a non-vacuum excitation has `k ≥ 1` crossings, and\n`k · E_×(q) ≥ E_×(q)`.  This is the constructive half of S1c\nstrategy (iii); the open half is the same statement for the\nphysical tower. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.crossingGradedTM_gapValue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.crossingGradedTM_gapValue","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CrossingGradedModel.lean#L73-L78","doc":"The model's gap value (first excited eigenvalue) is exactly one\ncrossing's energy. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.crossingGradedTM","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.crossingGradedTM","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CrossingGradedModel.lean#L51-L71","doc":"**The crossing-graded model transfer matrix**: the `k`-th\nexcitation carries exactly `k` crossings, each contributing the\nminimum crossing energy `E_×(q)`.  Parametrized over any direct\nlimit algebra and vacuum state (`vacuum_state_exists` supplies one\nfor every `dla`).\n\nThis is strategy (iii)'s additive energy accounting taken as the\n*definition* of the spectrum — a MODEL, not the physical\n`End(Aₙ)` spectrum (see module docstring). ","signatureChunk":0}]}